{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffKSLjiYoJ3WsTW3tdTS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written all three files for candidate 0, and the self-check prints `OK`. The fit is poor, though: it looks admissible but probably won't challenge the leading models.\n\n**The model: `random_vs_designed_exemplar_contrast`.** People keep two sets of remembered sequences of each length:\n- **Random-looking examples:** heads and tails balanced to within one, no streak longer than two, and no repeating unit.\n- **Designed examples:** any string made by repeating a short unit at least twice (HHHH, HTHT, HHTHHT, HHTTHHTT and so on).\n\nSimilarity to an example falls off exponentially with the number of flips that differ. A sequence looks random to the extent it resembles the random examples more than the designed ones, and people pick the sequence that scores higher. The fitted parameters are:\n- **How fast similarity falls off,** shared by everyone.\n- **How much the designed examples count,** also shared.\n- **How strongly each person acts on the comparison,** which varies by person and has spare slots so the next experiment's design can predict new participants.\n\n**Results:**\n- **Self-check:** it ran on the real responses, which include the person-level parameters, and printed `OK`. The ELPD-LOO from that short fit was -2669.7, about 300 nats behind the best model (-2369.5).\n- **Convergence:** a separate 4-chain fit (500 warm-up, 500 draws) had 0 divergences, R-hat ≤ 1.02 and bulk ESS ≥ 430. It took 135 s with all four chains on one CPU, so it should finish well inside the 30-minute limit.\n- **What it says about the theory:** the designed examples get almost no weight (about 0.06). Nearly all the fit comes from resembling the random examples, which says something about the exemplar idea itself.\n- **Reliability warning:** the short fit flagged 2.1% of trials with high Pareto-k, above the 1% tolerance, so the full fit's ELPD-LOO may be marked unreliable. That doesn't block admission, but such a model can't be exported as the winner.\n- **Not checked:** novelty against the other models. The earlier exemplar model, `exemplar_designed_pattern_similarity`, used only designed examples, so this one should not count as a duplicate of it.\n\nI tried fixing the designed-example weight at 1 to make it faster. That made the fit worse (-2871.0) and barely faster, so I put the weight back.\n\nFiles are in `.../experiment2/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_0/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1497,"cache_read_input_tokens":67838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1497,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b72248e8-1d89-47c7-b049-2e9e4dce72df","uuid":"c866bc19-c51e-4ede-87d1-818bbd8eaa8d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T12:39:56.679Z","request_id":"req_011CffKSKpef3ADvtPhbm3mP"}
